{"id":1269,"date":"2025-09-09T19:40:38","date_gmt":"2025-09-09T17:40:38","guid":{"rendered":"https:\/\/voyagermenorca.com\/elementor-1256\/"},"modified":"2026-07-02T13:21:35","modified_gmt":"2026-07-02T11:21:35","slug":"menorca-en-septiembre","status":"publish","type":"post","link":"https:\/\/voyagermenorca.com\/en\/menorca-en-septiembre\/","title":{"rendered":"Menorca in September"},"content":{"rendered":"\t\t<div data-elementor-type=\"wp-post\" data-elementor-id=\"1269\" class=\"elementor elementor-1269 elementor-1256\" data-elementor-post-type=\"post\">\n\t\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-0140b63 e-flex e-con-boxed e-con e-parent\" data-id=\"0140b63\" data-element_type=\"container\" data-e-type=\"container\">\n\t\t\t\t\t<div class=\"e-con-inner\">\n\t\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-ed091be elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\" data-id=\"ed091be\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"text-editor.default\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\n<article class=\"vm-post vm-post--biosfera\" lang=\"es\">\n  \n  <header class=\"vm-header\">\n    <h1>Menorca in September: 15 Quiet Plans and Local Guide Tips<\/h1>\n    <p class=\"vm-deck\">Fewer people, soft light, and perfect water for swimming. Real ideas to enjoy the island and connect with our guided tours of <strong>Ciutadella<\/strong> and <strong>Mah\u00f3n<\/strong>. <\/p>\n    <div class=\"vm-header-cta\">\n      <a class=\"vm-btn vm-btn--whatsapp\" href=\"https:\/\/wa.me\/34649902301\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">\ud83d\udcac Check schedules and book<\/a>\n <a class=\"vm-btn vm-btn--outline\" href=\"https:\/\/voyagermenorca.com\/en\/excursions\/\">\ud83d\udd0e See all excursions<\/a>\n    <\/div>\n  <\/header>\n\n  \n  <figure class=\"vm-figure\">\n    <img loading=\"lazy\" data-recalc-dims=\"1\" src=\"https:\/\/i0.wp.com\/images.pexels.com\/photos\/6007140\/pexels-photo-6007140.jpeg?resize=800%2C450&#038;ssl=1\" alt=\"Menorca in September: sunset at the Fav\u00e0ritx lighthouse\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"800\" height=\"450\">\n    <figcaption>Fav\u00e0ritx Lighthouse \u2022 Photo: Pexels<\/figcaption>\n  <\/figure>\n\n  \n  <nav class=\"vm-toc\" aria-label=\"Contenido\">\n    <strong>Content<\/strong>\n    <ol>\n      <li><a href=\"#por-que-septiembre\">What makes September special<\/a><\/li>\n      <li><a href=\"#calas\">Top 5 coves with fewer crowds<\/a><\/li>\n      <li><a href=\"#atardeceres\">Essential sunsets<\/a><\/li>\n      <li><a href=\"#ciutadella\">Ciutadella at sunset (with tour)<\/a><\/li>\n      <li><a href=\"#mahon\">Mah\u00f3n in the morning (with tour)<\/a><\/li>\n      <li><a href=\"#cami\">Cam\u00ed de Cavalls: 3 easy sections<\/a><\/li>\n      <li><a href=\"#talayot\">Talayotic for beginners<\/a><\/li>\n      <li><a href=\"#comer\">Eat well without queues<\/a><\/li>\n      <li><a href=\"#transporte\">Transportation and parking<\/a><\/li>\n      <li><a href=\"#mochila\">What to carry in your backpack<\/a><\/li>\n      <li><a href=\"#mapa\">Map with the 15 plans<\/a><\/li>\n      <li><a href=\"#faq\">Frequently Asked Questions<\/a><\/li>\n    <\/ol>\n  <\/nav>\n\n  \n  <section id=\"por-que-septiembre\" class=\"vm-section\">\n    <h2>1) What makes September special<\/h2>\n    <p>The island breathes after the peak of August: more availability, less traffic, and temperate sea. The afternoon light is perfect for photos in coves and historic centers. <\/p>\n    <p class=\"vm-inline-links\">\u2192 Learn why Menorca is a <a href=\"https:\/\/voyagermenorca.com\/en\/menorca-biosphere-reserve\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Biosphere Reserve<\/a>.<\/p>\n    <figure class=\"vm-figure\">\n      <img loading=\"lazy\" data-recalc-dims=\"1\" src=\"https:\/\/i0.wp.com\/images.pexels.com\/photos\/29104816\/pexels-photo-29104816.jpeg?resize=800%2C534&#038;ssl=1\" alt=\"Street with traditional architecture in Ciutadella de Menorca at sunset\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"800\" height=\"534\">\n      <figcaption>Ciutadella at sunset \u2022 Photo: Pexels<\/figcaption>\n    <\/figure>\n  <\/section>\n\n  \n  <section id=\"calas\" class=\"vm-section\">\n    <h2>2) Top 5 coves with fewer crowds<\/h2>\n    <p>Wake up a little early and you&#8217;ll have an almost private setting. Five balanced options between beauty and access: <\/p>\n    <div class=\"vm-gallery\">\n      <figure>\n        <img loading=\"lazy\" data-recalc-dims=\"1\" src=\"https:\/\/i0.wp.com\/images.pexels.com\/photos\/13717494\/pexels-photo-13717494.jpeg?resize=800%2C533&#038;ssl=1\" alt=\"Cala Galdana from the viewpoint with pine trees, Menorca\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"800\" height=\"533\">\n        <figcaption>Cala Galdana<\/figcaption>\n      <\/figure>\n      <figure>\n        <img loading=\"lazy\" data-recalc-dims=\"1\" src=\"https:\/\/i0.wp.com\/images.pexels.com\/photos\/32218229\/pexels-photo-32218229.jpeg?resize=800%2C533&#038;ssl=1\" alt=\"Cala Pilar on the north coast of Menorca\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"800\" height=\"533\">\n        <figcaption>Cala Pilar<\/figcaption>\n      <\/figure>\n      <figure>\n        <img loading=\"lazy\" data-recalc-dims=\"1\" src=\"https:\/\/i0.wp.com\/images.pexels.com\/photos\/9510812\/pexels-photo-9510812.jpeg?resize=800%2C533&#038;ssl=1\" alt=\"Cliffs and sea on the coast of Ciutadella de Menorca\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"800\" height=\"533\">\n        <figcaption>Coast of Ciutadella<\/figcaption>\n      <\/figure>\n    <\/div>\n    <ul class=\"vm-list\">\n      <li><strong>Algaiarens (La Vall):<\/strong> easy access and intense green tones.<\/li>\n      <li><strong>Cavalleria:<\/strong> reddish sand, nearby lighthouse for sunset.<\/li>\n      <li><strong>Cala Pilar:<\/strong> wild; ideal with a light tramontana.<\/li>\n      <li><strong>Binigaus:<\/strong> wide sandy area for walking at the end of the day.<\/li>\n      <li><strong>Es Grau:<\/strong> family-friendly and with a link to the <em>Cam\u00ed de Cavalls<\/em>.<\/li>\n    <\/ul>\n    <p class=\"vm-inline-links\">\u2192 Practical guide: <a href=\"https:\/\/voyagermenorca.com\/en\/the-best-beaches-in-menorca-and-which-ones-to-avoid-in-high-season\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Best beaches in Menorca and which ones to avoid<\/a>.<\/p>\n  <\/section>\n\n  \n  <section id=\"atardeceres\" class=\"vm-section\">\n    <h2>3) Essential sunsets<\/h2>\n    <ol class=\"vm-steps\">\n      <li><strong>Pont d\u2019en Gil<\/strong> (Ciutadella): photogenic natural arch.<\/li>\n      <li><strong>Faro de Cavalleria<\/strong>: clear horizon and north coast.<\/li>\n      <li><strong>Faro de Artrutx<\/strong>: iconic silhouette with restaurants.<\/li>\n    <\/ol>\n    <p class=\"vm-inline-links\">\u2192 Complete your route: <a href=\"https:\/\/voyagermenorca.com\/en\/the-7-lighthouses-of-menorca\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">The 7 lighthouses of Menorca<\/a>.<\/p>\n    <figure class=\"vm-figure\">\n      <img loading=\"lazy\" data-recalc-dims=\"1\" src=\"https:\/\/i0.wp.com\/images.pexels.com\/photos\/16565376\/pexels-photo-16565376.jpeg?resize=800%2C450&#038;ssl=1\" alt=\"Cavalleria lighthouse with clear sky at sunset, Menorca\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"800\" height=\"450\">\n      <figcaption>Cavalleria Lighthouse \u2022 Photo: Pexels<\/figcaption>\n    <\/figure>\n  <\/section>\n\n  \n  <section id=\"ciutadella\" class=\"vm-section\">\n    <h2>4) Ciutadella at sunset: historic center and photogenic corners<\/h2>\n    <p>Our <strong>guided tour of Ciutadella<\/strong> covers Pla\u00e7a des Born, the Cathedral, mar\u00e8s alleys, and viewpoints to the port. Photo tips and \u201csecret\u201d stops. <\/p>\n    <figure class=\"vm-figure\">\n      <img loading=\"lazy\" data-recalc-dims=\"1\" src=\"https:\/\/i0.wp.com\/images.pexels.com\/photos\/32849451\/pexels-photo-32849451.jpeg?resize=800%2C534&#038;ssl=1\" alt=\"Rocky shore and turquoise waters in Ciutadella de Menorca\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"800\" height=\"534\">\n      <figcaption>Shore in Ciutadella \u2022 Photo: Pexels<\/figcaption>\n    <\/figure>\n    <p class=\"vm-cta-inline\">\n      <a class=\"vm-btn vm-btn--primary\" href=\"https:\/\/voyagermenorca.com\/en\/excursions\/\">\ud83d\udd14 Book a visit in Ciutadella<\/a>\n <a class=\"vm-btn vm-btn--outline\" href=\"https:\/\/wa.me\/34649902301\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">\ud83d\udcac Ask by WhatsApp<\/a>\n    <\/p>\n  <\/section>\n\n  \n  <section id=\"mahon\" class=\"vm-section\">\n    <h2>5) Mah\u00f3n in the morning: port, viewpoints, and market<\/h2>\n    <p>The <strong>port of Ma\u00f3<\/strong> shines with the light of the early hours. On the tour, we visit viewpoints, the market, and streets with stories of corsairs and merchants. <\/p>\n    <figure class=\"vm-figure\">\n      <img loading=\"lazy\" data-recalc-dims=\"1\" src=\"https:\/\/i0.wp.com\/images.pexels.com\/photos\/17422240\/pexels-photo-17422240.jpeg?resize=800%2C534&#038;ssl=1\" alt=\"View of Mediterranean port with boats, Menorca\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"800\" height=\"534\">\n      <figcaption>Port (reference) \u2022 Photo: Pexels<\/figcaption>\n    <\/figure>\n    <p class=\"vm-cta-inline\">\n      <a class=\"vm-btn vm-btn--primary\" href=\"https:\/\/voyagermenorca.com\/en\/excursions\/\">\ud83e\udded Book a visit in Mah\u00f3n<\/a>\n <a class=\"vm-btn vm-btn--outline\" href=\"https:\/\/voyagermenorca.com\/en\/excursions\/\">\ud83d\udd0e See all excursions<\/a>\n    <\/p>\n  <\/section>\n\n  \n  <section id=\"cami\" class=\"vm-section\">\n    <h2>6) Cam\u00ed de Cavalls: 3 easy sections for half a day<\/h2>\n    <ul class=\"vm-cards\">\n      <li>\n        <h3>Es Grau \u2192 Faro de Fav\u00e0ritx (partial)<\/h3>\n        <p>3\u20136 km (adaptable). Walkways and wetlands; ideal with children. <\/p>\n      <\/li>\n      <li>\n        <h3>Algaiarens \u2192 Cala Pilar (partial)<\/h3>\n        <p>6\u20138 km. Forest, dunes, and viewpoints. Bring water.  <\/p>\n      <\/li>\n      <li>\n        <h3>Son Saura \u2192 Cala en Turqueta<\/h3>\n        <p>5\u20137 km. South coast, intermittent shade, and turquoise coves. <\/p>\n      <\/li>\n    <\/ul>\n    <figure class=\"vm-figure\">\n      <img loading=\"lazy\" data-recalc-dims=\"1\" src=\"https:\/\/i0.wp.com\/images.pexels.com\/photos\/32207396\/pexels-photo-32207396.jpeg?resize=800%2C534&#038;ssl=1\" alt=\"Wooden sign to Cal\u00f3 Fondo on the coast of Ciutadella\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"800\" height=\"534\">\n      <figcaption>Sign on coastal path \u2022 Photo: Pexels<\/figcaption>\n    <\/figure>\n  <\/section>\n\n  \n  <section id=\"talayot\" class=\"vm-section\">\n    <h2>7) Talayotic for beginners<\/h2>\n    <p>To start, combine <strong>Naveta des Tudons<\/strong> with a Talayotic settlement (Torralba d\u2019en Salort or Talat\u00ed de Dalt). In 2\u20133 hours you will understand taulas, talayots, and navetas. <\/p>\n    <figure class=\"vm-figure\">\n      <img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"https:\/\/commons.wikimedia.org\/wiki\/Special:FilePath\/Naveta%20des%20Tudons%20-%20001.jpg\" alt=\"Naveta des Tudons in Ciutadella, Menorca\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"1600\" height=\"1067\">\n      <figcaption>Naveta des Tudons \u2022 Photo: Wikimedia Commons (CC BY-SA)<\/figcaption>\n    <\/figure>\n  <\/section>\n\n  \n  <section id=\"comer\" class=\"vm-section\">\n    <h2>8) Eat well without queues<\/h2>\n    <ul class=\"vm-list\">\n      <li>Book a table for 13:00\u201313:30 or 20:00\u201320:30.<\/li>\n      <li>Ask for local dishes: caldereta, oliaigua, Mah\u00f3n-Menorca DOP cheese.<\/li>\n      <li>In small towns, confirm hours outside of weekends.<\/li>\n    <\/ul>\n    <figure class=\"vm-figure\">\n      <img loading=\"lazy\" data-recalc-dims=\"1\" src=\"https:\/\/i0.wp.com\/images.pexels.com\/photos\/33484279\/pexels-photo-33484279.jpeg?resize=800%2C534&#038;ssl=1\" alt=\"Steaming seafood stew in black pot (reference)\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"800\" height=\"534\">\n      <figcaption>Seafood stew (reference) \u2022 Photo: Pexels<\/figcaption>\n    <\/figure>\n  <\/section>\n\n  \n  <section id=\"transporte\" class=\"vm-section\">\n    <h2>9) Transportation and parking in September<\/h2>\n    <p>The bus works well to main centers; for more remote coves, car or taxi. Arrive early to the parking lots of southern beaches if the day is very stable. <\/p>\n  <\/section>\n\n  \n  <section id=\"mochila\" class=\"vm-section\">\n    <h2>10) What to carry in your backpack<\/h2>\n    <ul class=\"vm-checklist\">\n      <li>Water (1\u20131.5 L per person) and something salty.<\/li>\n      <li>Cap, glasses, and sunscreen.<\/li>\n      <li>Closed shoes for the trail and flip-flops for the cove.<\/li>\n      <li>Light towel and waste bag.<\/li>\n      <li>Headlamp\/flashlight if you return after sunset.<\/li>\n    <\/ul>\n  <\/section>\n\n  \n  <section id=\"mapa\" class=\"vm-section\">\n    <h2>11) Map with the 15 plans<\/h2>\n    <p>We have marked coves, lighthouses, viewpoints, and points of our tours. Use it to organize your days. <\/p>\n    \n    <div class=\"vm-mapwrap\">\n      <iframe src=\"https:\/\/www.google.com\/maps\/d\/embed?mid=16AJzsa_43Jks1nhu9DG2gXcWBDFDCv8&amp;ehbc=2E312F\" width=\"100%\" height=\"480\" style=\"border:0\" loading=\"lazy\" allowfullscreen=\"\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer-when-downgrade\"><\/iframe>\n    <\/div>\n  <\/section>\n\n  \n  <section id=\"faq\" class=\"vm-section\">\n    <h2>12) Frequently Asked Questions<\/h2>\n    <details class=\"vm-faq\">\n      <summary>Is it hot in Menorca in September?<\/summary>\n      <p>During the first half of the month it is usually mild and nights are cooler. Bring a light layer for sunset. <\/p>\n    <\/details>\n    <details class=\"vm-faq\">\n      <summary>Can you still swim?<\/summary>\n      <p>Yes, the sea temperature is usually excellent in September, ideal for long sessions without feeling cold.<\/p>\n    <\/details>\n    <details class=\"vm-faq\">\n      <summary>Which sections of the Cam\u00ed de Cavalls are easier?<\/summary>\n      <p>Es Grau\u2013Fav\u00e0ritx (partial), Son Saura\u2013Cala en Turqueta and the surroundings of Algaiarens combine good footing and landscapes.<\/p>\n    <\/details>\n    <details class=\"vm-faq\">\n      <summary>How to get around without a car?<\/summary>\n      <p>Use the bus between centers and combine with a taxi for coves. To get to know the city, book our <a href=\"https:\/\/voyagermenorca.com\/en\/excursions\/\">guided tours<\/a>. <\/p>\n    <\/details>\n    <details class=\"vm-faq\">\n      <summary>Do I need to book restaurants?<\/summary>\n      <p>Recommended, especially on weekends. During the week, there is usually availability at the beginning of service. <\/p>\n    <\/details>\n  <\/section>\n\n  \n  <p class=\"vm-cta-inline vm-cta-inline--final\">\n    <a class=\"vm-btn vm-btn--whatsapp\" href=\"https:\/\/wa.me\/34649902301\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">\ud83d\udcac Chat on WhatsApp<\/a>\n    <a class=\"vm-btn vm-btn--outline\" href=\"https:\/\/voyagermenorca.com\/en\/excursions\/\">\ud83d\udd0e See excursions<\/a>\n    <a class=\"vm-btn vm-btn--outline\" href=\"https:\/\/voyagermenorca.com\/en\/the-7-lighthouses-of-menorca\/\">\ud83c\udf05 Lighthouses of Menorca<\/a>\n    <a class=\"vm-btn vm-btn--outline\" href=\"https:\/\/voyagermenorca.com\/en\/the-best-beaches-in-menorca-and-which-ones-to-avoid-in-high-season\/\">\ud83c\udfd6\ufe0f Best beaches<\/a>\n  <\/p>\n<\/article>\n\n\n<style>\n  :root{\n    --vm-ink:#0b1220; --vm-muted:#5b667a; --vm-bg:#fff;\n    --vm-brand:#00c2a8; --vm-brand-2:#2aa3ff; --vm-border:#e6e9ef; --vm-radius:16px;\n  }\n  .vm-post{color:var(--vm-ink);font:16px\/1.65 system-ui,-apple-system,Segoe UI,Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,\"Apple Color Emoji\",\"Segoe UI Emoji\";}\n  .vm-header h1{font-size:clamp(1.6r